Peering into the Dark Wind, Magi study the patterns beneath matter, memory,
light, distance, heat, death, and spellwork itself. They keep those patterns in
leather-bound spellbooks and carry them into the field, where a good idea can
become a fireball, a hidden path, a stolen moment, or a way home.

Mage is a broad spellcasting guild with a gentle first page and considerable
room to grow. Mana Shard and Missile give a new member dependable attacks;
Analyze, Detect, and Blaze make the same character useful while exploring.
Fighting suitable enemies earns Mage GXP, and useful field magic awards 10 GXP
for a utility working or 20 for a combat working, at most once per working
every thirty seconds. That GXP raises Arcane through fifteen ranks and reveals
new workings along the way.

The spellbook grows through use as well as rank. Individual workings become
Practiced, Fluent, Inscribed, and Instinctive, opening lower costs, rune
sockets, and automatic barrage casting. A Mage can prepare a Practiced combat
working to fire alongside ordinary attacks. Wielding a FOCUS weapon opens that
style immediately and channels the automatic spell for no SP; adding worn AURA
equipment creates full battlemage resonance, improving its speed and force.
Investiture, learned at Arcane 4, can temporarily supply either quality but not
both at once.

Runes change the character of a familiar working. Some are part of ordinary
study, while others appear only after the spellbook has witnessed enough
mastery, fire, or stranger discoveries. The deepest trail returns to the
ruined Isle of the Magi, where the broken Tower of Arcanarton still remembers
the war that separated Mage and Necromancer lore.

GXP continues to matter after the fifteenth Arcane rank. Long study opens new
styles of marginalia, giving completed workings a visible signature without
turning those flourishes into another compulsory source of power.

Prospective Magi need at least 6 Intelligence. Speak with Merlin here to join;
afterward, open the new spellbook with "spellbook" and let "research" point
toward the next page.
